    <string name="rtmp_method_title">RTMP: Players and media servers</string>
    <string name="rtmp_method_summary">Watch in a video player, or send the stream to a media server.</string>
    <string name="rtmp_method_conditions">Compatible RTMP software · Optional audio</string>
    <string name="rtmp_method_intro">RTMP is a common streaming standard used by video players and media servers. By default, this device hosts the stream. You can also send it to a media server.</string>
    <string-array name="rtmp_method_benefits">
        <item>Watch in players such as VLC by opening the RTMP address shown in the app.</item>
        <item>Send the stream to a media server, including servers that ask for a username and password.</item>
        <item>Add microphone audio, device audio, or both.</item>
        <item>Choose video and audio formats, size and quality to suit your player or server.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="rtmp_method_things_to_know">
        <item>Players must be able to connect to this device, for example on the same Wi-Fi. Hosting works without internet.</item>
        <item>When sending to a server, this device must be able to reach it. For an encrypted connection, use an rtmps:// address. The format is rtmp://host/app/streamKey.</item>
        <item>Your player or server must support the formats you choose. H.264 with AAC works everywhere; H.265 needs Enhanced RTMP support.</item>
    </string-array>

